# telemetry.phext — deploy telemetry

Will's order (2026-11-22): "ensure telemetry from deploys flows
to telemetry.phext in exo-plan."

The flow: deploy-all.sh (the one-command awsbox deploy roll-up)
emits one plain-text record per run into ~/telemetry-outbox/ on
awsbox, as its final step — best-effort, never gating, never
changing the run's exit code. ~/bin/telemetry-push.sh ships every
pending record to aletheia-core over SSH (dedicated key, the
phdoc push pattern) and deletes a local copy only after the hub
confirms ingest. ~/telemetry-receive.sh on the hub ingests the
records into ~/workspace/phext/telemetry-records/ (one file per
run-id, deduped by run-id), rebuilds this phext with
~/workspace/phext/build_telemetry_phext.py, and lands it here in
wbic16/exo-plan@exo through a dedicated clone — fetch first,
never force, remote head verified after push.

Coordinate scheme: this Home scroll at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1; one
scroll per run at 1.1.1/1.1.2/1.1.<n>, n the run's sequence
number in run-id order (run-ids open with a UTC timestamp, so
the order is chronological and a run's coordinate never
changes). The builder documents the scheme in full.

